y":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0028850753378116822,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":53.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.017329972863526194,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":71.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.023559999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":15.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Driven Brands Holdings Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides automotive services to retail and commercial customers in the United States and Canada. The company operates through Take 5, Franchise Brands, and Auto Glass Now segments. It offers various services, such as paint, collision, glass, repair, and oil change; maintenance services including differential fluid exchanges, coolant services and air and cabin filters; and auto glass and windshield replacement, repair, and calibration services. The company also distributes automotive parts, including radiators, air conditioning components, and exhaust products to automotive repair shops, auto parts stores, body shops, and other auto repair outlets. In addition, it provides training services to repair and maintenance, and paint and collision shops. It sells its products and services under the ABRA, CARSTAR, MAACO, Meineke Car Care Centers, PH Vitres D'Auto, Take 5 Oil Change, Auto Glass Now, Fix Auto, and 1-800-Radiator & A/C, Uniban, and Automotive Training Institute brand names. The company was founded in 1972 and is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel R. Rivera J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $766,936 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $262K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Driven Brands Holdings Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.0B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $108M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Driven Brands (NASDAQ:DRVN) Cut to Neutral at BTIG Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/driven-brands-nasdaqdrvn-cut-to-neutral-at-btig-research.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793794027.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Driven Brands (NASDAQ:DRVN) Shares Gap Down \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/driven-brands-nasdaqdrvn-shares-gap-down-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793721778.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of DRVN and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Behavioral_Patterns_of_DRVN_and_Institutional_Flows_103126085801_1793494681.html","date":"2026-11-01","